{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>YHWH came from Sinai.</b> It should have said 'at Sinai,' and likewise 'at Seir, at Mount Paran,' and the commentators explained that the mem in place of the bet. But it seems to me that had it said 'at Sinai,' it would have implied place for the blessed Name — and know that He is the place of His world, but His world is not His place — in the manner that the Sages of blessed memory expounded (Psalms 68:18): ״אדני בם סיני בקדש״ — it does not say 'the Sanctuary at Sinai,' but rather 'Sinai in the Sanctuary'; and therefore he needed to say 'from Sinai he came,' that is, from Sinai He was revealed to Israel, for from there the Glory began to come into Israel. And he proceeds to explain how: that at first 'He shone forth from Seir to them,' for Seir was far from Sinai, since Israel did not come to the wilderness of Seir until the end, when they came to the border of the children of Esau, and afterward the Glory went from Seir to Mount Paran, which was close to Sinai, for from Paran Moses sent the spies, and from Paran they came to Sinai, and from Sinai to Israel — and this is 'from Sinai he came.' And Scripture mentioned the last one first, because it is the ultimate purpose of the intention, to come to it. And behold, Devorah the prophetess explained the matter to us, for she said (Judges 5:4): ״ה' בצאתך משעיר בצעדך משדה אדום״ and so on — this is Sinai, before YHWH, the God of Israel." "<b>And you should be roused</b> concerning the fact that he used the term זרח ('shone forth') for Seir, which was far, a word denoting the beginning of shining, and for Paran, which was close, the term הופיע ('appeared'), for then the brilliance of the Glory spread and grew as it drew near Sinai; and for Sinai itself he used the term בא ('came'), because the ultimate intention was upon it, and it is the mountain Elohim desired for His dwelling (Psalms 68:17), and from there He was revealed before the eyes of all Israel." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'YHWH came from Sinai and shone forth from Seir' — He opened to the children of Seir that they should receive the Torah and they did not want to; 'He appeared from Mount Paran' — He went from there and opened to the children of Ishmael that they should receive it and they did not want to, and He came to Israel. Scripture mentioned all the seed of Abraham, for none wished to receive the Torah except Israel, the seed of Jacob alone. And the fact that He mentioned Esau and Ishmael applies by the same reasoning to all the other nations, and likewise the Sages of blessed memory expounded: the Holy One, blessed be He, went around to every nation and tongue and they did not accept it, until Israel came and accepted it." "<b>From His right hand, a fiery law to them.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'from His right hand' it was — He showed him supernal fire and made the law heard to Israel, not from the right hand of the angels just mentioned, but the Holy One, blessed be He, Himself in His Glory; and it is as if it said 'fire and law.'" "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah,</b> one may say: 'from His right hand' — He made the law heard to them, to Israel, from within the fire, for this was the apprehension of Israel; but Moses heard from His right hand literally. And perhaps to allude to this, these two words — אש דת — come as a single word in a Torah scroll, for it is the rule of a Torah scroll that they be one word, in order to join דת to אש and to establish in the heart that the law which He made heard to them from within the fire — that they heard it. And thus it is written (Deuteronomy 4:15): ״ביום דבר ה' אליכם בחורב מתוך האש״, and I have already mentioned this in the verse 'and He spoke,' and a similar instance we find among the Prophets (Jeremiah 6:29): ״נחר מפוח מאשתם עופרת״ — one word, thus written in the Masorah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:56.516882615Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}